eriods of heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; San Juan River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.002.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued September 22 at 9:44AM MDT until September 25 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...A portion of southwest Colorado, including the following\nareas, San Juan River Basin and Southwest San Juan Mountains.\n\n* WHEN...From Wednesday afternoon through late Thursday night.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- The ground remains saturated from recent heavy rainfall over the\npast week. After a brief break, deep moisture is expected to\nreturn to southwest Colorado Tuesday with a few inches of\nrainfall possible during the Wednesday through Thursday\ntimeframe. In addition, multiple rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms are expected Wednesday through Thursday evening\nproducing periods of heavy rainfall and potential flash flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-25T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Animas River Basin","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.c86447dd54a169ae9df7d6c5b6b9b0c629575548.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-22T19:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221948 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 148 PM MDT Tue Sep 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Wetter weather returns to the region today, with showers and storms possible each day through the end of the work week. - There is a potential for moderate and heavy rainfall that could lead to flooding mainly in the southern San Juans and surrounding vall","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-22T19:54:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Moisture returns today with increased chances for showers and thunderstorms. The best chances for wetting rains will be over the central and southern Colorado mountains, but any higher terrain will see the possibility for a shower or thunderstorm. Precip chances and increased relative humidity continues through week keeping critical fire weather conditions at a minimum. ...GUSTY ERRA","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"drg01","station_name":"Durango","distance_km":18.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f":66.47,"soil_temp_15cm_f":70.41,"soil_moisture_5cm":null,"soil_moisture_15cm":null,"precip_in":null,"eto_in":null,"vapor_pressure":null,"solar_radiation":608.67,"wind_speed_mph":6.54,"air_temp_f":69.28,"relative_humidity":0.58,"url":"https://coagmet.colostate.edu/station/drg01"},"aviation":{"icao":"KDRO","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"SPECI KDRO 222024Z AUTO 06006KT 10SM FEW024 SCT047 BKN075 20/08 A3021 RMK AO2 PK WND 14028/1957 LTG DSNT S-W RAE09 TSE20 P0000 T02000078","temp_f":68,"wind_dir":60,"wind_kt":6,"gust_kt":null,"visibility":"10+","cover":"BKN","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1023.1,"observed":1790108640,"raw_taf":"TAF KDRO 221733Z 2218/2318 05004KT P6SM SCT050 BKN250 PROB30 2218/2221 4SM -TSRA BKN050CB FM222100 15009KT 6SM -SHRA SCT060 BKN120 PROB30 2221/2303 4SM TSRA BKN060CB FM230400 08007KT 6SM -SHRA SCT020 OVC030 FM231400 VRB03KT P6SM SCT030 OVC050 PROB30 2314/2318 4SM SHRA","url":"https://aviationweather.gov/data/metar/?ids=KDRO&hours=0"},"airgradient":null,"airnow":{"aqi":42,"category":"Good","pa